  "question": {
    "text": "A vector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> in the first octant is inclined to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>-axis at an acute angle. If a plane passing through the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, is normal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, then",
    "image": null
